Before reinstalling SR-IOV

First, verify there are no leftover SR-IOV resources:

oc get crd | grep sriov

oc get sriovnetworknodestate -A

oc get sriovnetworknodepolicy -A

oc get sriovoperatorconfig -A

If those are clean (or if you intentionally remove any leftovers), you can reinstall the SR-IOV Operator.

Since the previous installation became stuck during the drain process, I'd also recommend checking the cluster version before reinstalling:

oc get clusterversion
oc get co

If all ClusterOperators are Available=True and Degraded=False, the cluster is in a good state for another SR-IOV installation attempt.

